# Belligerent Yearling: only "another Dinosaur you control" triggers it (CR 603.2c) - Bot1's own Ornithopter (not a Dinosaur) and Bot2's Giant Cindermaw (not under Bot1's control) enter
# without any question. The base power is set to the entering creature's power, not raised to it: on turn 3 Bot1 casts a Nest Robber (a 2/1 Dinosaur), accepts, and the Yearling is a 2/2.

[Bot1 Deck]
Black Lotus
Mox Ruby
Mox Jet
Belligerent Yearling
Ornithopter
Nest Robber
Plains x14

[Bot2 Deck]
Black Lotus
Giant Cindermaw
Island x18

[Actions]
Bot1.Hand.Black Lotus.Cast
Bot1.Hand.Mox Ruby.Cast
Bot1.Hand.Mox Jet.Cast
Bot1.Battlefield.Black Lotus.Activate(Color: Red)
Bot1.Hand.Belligerent Yearling.Cast
Bot1.Hand.Ornithopter.Cast
Bot1.Pass
Bot2.Pass
? Stack.Count = 0
? Bot1.Battlefield.Belligerent Yearling.Power = 3
[T2 Bot2.Main1]
Bot2.Hand.Black Lotus.Cast
Bot2.Battlefield.Black Lotus.Activate(Color: Red)
Bot2.Hand.Giant Cindermaw.Cast
Bot2.Pass
Bot1.Pass
? Stack.Count = 0
? Bot1.Battlefield.Belligerent Yearling.Power = 3
[T3 Bot1.Main1]
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Ruby.Activate
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Jet.Activate
Bot1.Hand.Nest Robber.Cast
Bot1.Pass
Bot2.Pass
Bot1.Accept
? Bot1.Battlefield.Belligerent Yearling.Power = 2

[Expect]
Bot1.Battlefield.Belligerent Yearling.Toughness = 2
